 ## The world
 
-The world is one seeded railway that runs on forever, with terrain around it, towns every few thousand tiles and trains on a seeded timetable. You find the track, scout or wait, and pick a train, sometimes the wrong or a tougher one. You find trains by their smoke and whistles, and tell train types apart by sight once there are several types; later by rumours and timetables too. At dusk you pick a camp off the line, and tomorrow starts from there. Each career gets a new world.
+The world is one seeded railway that runs on forever, with terrain around it, towns every few thousand tiles and trains on a seeded timetable. You find the track, scout or wait, and pick a train, sometimes the wrong or a tougher one. You find trains by their smoke and whistles, and tell train types apart by sight once there are several types; later by rumours and timetables too. At dusk you race the light to a camp off the line, and tomorrow starts from there. Picking a good camp is part of the day: a bad one means a long ride to tomorrow's trains, and later a posse may find it. Each career gets a new world.
 
 Trains run one way first, and both ways once passing loops exist. Forks come later, leading into regions with different trains. Something has to stop you riding off the side of the line: see [Map edges](Map-edges).
 
